    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d152">

                <pb facs="0222" n="106" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg106"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.51/701.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The British Ambassador to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">British Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1911-12-18">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 18, 1911</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Knox</hi>: There seems to be some
                    difference of opinion among the representatives of the six powers at Peking
                    regarding the <pb facs="0223" n="107" xml:id="pg107"/> desirability of making
                    the loan proposed to Yuan Shih Kai unless the revolutionaries agree, which it
                    seems they will not do, and my Government would like to know your view of the
                    position before a final decision is reached.</p>
                <p>Believe me [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">James Bryce</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
